{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/138285": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Constituent Programs",
      "description": "Associate Director of Constituent Programs You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Associate Director of Constituent Programs Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,000.00 - $75,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: The Associate Director of Constituent Programs leads the planning, execution, and evaluation of engagement programs designed to foster connections between students, alumni, parents, employees and friends and Western New England University. This position is responsible for the successful management of volunteer groups including the Student Alumni Association, the Parents Council, and various alumni groups. It also manages events, including Golden Bear Weekend, reunion celebrations, the Annual Alumni Awards, the Alumni Golf Tournament, regional engagement events, alumni volunteer programs, and alumni board initiatives. Working collaboratively with Advancement colleagues and campus partners, the Associate Director develops and implements strategies that strengthen relationships, increase constituent engagement and participation, and support the University's mission and goals. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: Reporting to the Director of Strategic Engagement, the Associate Director of Constituent Programs serves as the primary manager of the University's engagement programs and experiences, creating meaningful opportunities for students, alumni, parents and friends to connect with one another and with Western New England University. Through the strategic planning and execution of signature events, volunteer initiatives, volunteer leadership activities, regional programming, and reunion efforts, the Associate Director fosters lifelong relationships that strengthen affinity and participation. This role collaborates closely with Advancement colleagues, campus partners, and volunteers to identify engagement opportunities, cultivate involvement, and deliver programs that reflect the diverse interests and experiences of the University's volunteer communities. By leveraging relationship-building, volunteer management, technology, and engagement best practices, the Associate Director helps advance institutional priorities and supports a culture of connection, engagement, and philanthropy. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Program Development Spearhead the growth of the Parent’s Council through communications and events. Launch a Student Alumni Association in order to foster closer connections between current students and alumni. Execute with the support of the Director in delivering a robust calendar of events, including engagement, cultivation, stewardship and recognition events, to drive engagement among alumni, students, and other constituents, and to support the strategic priorities of the Advancement Division and the University. Work collaboratively with Advancement and University Marketing to create engaging, thoughtful communications - both print and digital - to support events and initiatives. Serve as the primary manager for the annual Alumni Awards and Law Alumni Awards processes, including event marketing and logistics, sponsor recruitment, managing honoree selection and their experiences, registration, etc. Serve as primary manager for signature events such as Golden Bear Weekend, the Alumni Golf Tournament, Golden Graduates reunion, and more. Spearhead sponsorship solicitation, participant recruitment, and event logistics for Alumni Association signature programs including Golden Bear Weekend and Alumni Golf Tournament. Plan, direct, and execute programs and initiatives (e.g., career networking/development opportunities for current students and alumni, Golden Bear Weekend, regional/national alumni events, reunion programs) that help the University meet key alumni engagement goals. Manage the development of regional, affinity, and school/college programs and events to drive engagement of alumni in key geographical areas and targeted constituencies such as professional programs, academic- or industry-based affinities, athletics, non-athletic student activities, and more. Spearhead efforts to expand digital alumni engagement opportunities, including current and future technologies to support a variety of online engagement including online communities, online networking/mentoring, virtual events, etc. Manage volunteer programs including recruitment and management for a variety of alumni volunteer programs, including micro-volunteering, event volunteering, and committee-level volunteering. Work closely with and coordinate all activities of the Alumni Association Board and its committees, including ensuring a robust agenda for meetings that continually addresses strategies to increase alumni engagement. Facilitate the involvement of current students in alumni engagement activities prior to graduation (including mentoring, internship, and job opportunities). Broadly communicate the advantages of involvement. Ensure accurate and complete alumni database records by capturing contact, biographical, and career information of alumni. Relationship Management Collaborate with and support a variety of campus partners as assigned. Serve as the staff liaison to Alumni Board Committees as assigned by the Director. MARGINAL DUTIES: Work effectively and in a cooperative manner with all University employees and constituencies. Participate in University functions and committee/teamwork, as appropriate. Represent the University as appropriate. Perform other functions as assigned. Qualifications QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Bachelor’s Degree required 1-3 years of professional experience required; prior experience in higher education, alumni relations or fundraising preferred Demonstrated knowledge of and experience in event management Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills Valid driver’s license REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Ability to work cooperatively with various constituencies, including diverse populations of alumni, faculty, staff, students, parents, and community leaders Ability to plan and execute programs, managing projects in a high-volume, deadline-driven environment Knowledge of and experience in alumni engagement, volunteer management, and special events Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing Demonstrated proficiency with computers, especially Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint; familiarity with constituent software (CRM Advance) ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Sitting, standing, bending, walking, climbing stairs and reaching as expected in normal office setting Occasional lifting, not to exceed 25 pounds Operation of computer keyboard and use of CRT HOURS: Minimum of 40 hours per week Flexible schedule according to the needs of the department Ability to work nights and weekends, as needed Ability to travel, as needed Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/137940": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Neuroscience",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Neuroscience You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Visiting Assistant Professor of Neuroscience Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $70,000.00 - $80,000.00 Salary Position Type Faculty Education Level Doctoral Degree Apply Description Visiting Assistant Professor of Neuroscience Western New England University | College of Arts and Sciences The College of Arts and Sciences at Western New England University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Visiting Assistant Professor of Neuroscience beginning in Spring 2027. The position will support the University's interdisciplinary undergraduate Neuroscience program as its academic administration transitions to the College of Arts and Sciences. The appointment will be housed in the Department of Psychology or the Department of Physical and Biological Sciences, depending on the successful candidate's disciplinary expertise. The position carries a 4/4 teaching load (12 instructional credits per semester), with the possibility of administrative course release for assigned responsibilities such as curriculum review and redesign, laboratory or research coordination, or other program-transition needs. Immediate Spring 2027 teaching priorities include Sensation and Perception, Cognitive Neuroscience, Neurodevelopment, and an upper-level Neuroscience elective or special-topics course appropriate to the candidate's expertise. Future assignments may include Introduction to Behavioral Neuroscience, Research Methods in Neuroscience, Neurobiology, Seminar in Neuroscience, and other upper-level courses. Exact assignments will reflect the candidate's background and program needs. The successful candidate will also contribute to student mentoring and academic planning, including course sequencing and degree progress during the transition. The position will help coordinate undergraduate research experiences by connecting students with appropriate faculty mentors and, where appropriate, supervising research rotations, placements, independent study, or senior thesis work. Opportunities exist to collaborate across Psychology, Biological Sciences, Health Sciences, Pharmacy, and related fields. A Ph.D. in Neuroscience or a closely related field is preferred. Advanced ABD candidates expecting to complete the doctorate by or near the beginning of the appointment may also be considered. Candidates should be prepared to teach across multiple areas of the undergraduate Neuroscience curriculum and demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring. Prior college-level teaching, undergraduate research mentoring, laboratory instruction, curriculum development, or academic advising is desirable. The anticipated annual salary range is $70,000-$80,000, subject to HR review and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants should submit a cover letter describing their qualifications and the Neuroscience areas or courses they are prepared to teach, a current curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Official transcripts of higher-education coursework will be required prior to appointment; unofficial transcripts may be submitted with the initial application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Neuroscience or a closely related field is preferred. Advanced ABD candidates expecting to complete the doctorate by or near the beginning of the appointment may also be considered. Candidates should be prepared to teach across multiple areas of the undergraduate Neuroscience curriculum and demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentoring. Prior college-level teaching, undergraduate research mentoring, laboratory instruction, curriculum development, or academic advising is desirable. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/137323": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Construction Management Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $92,000.00 - $100,000.00 Salary Position Type Faculty Education Level Doctoral Degree Apply Description Assistant Professor of Construction Management The Construction Management Program at Western New England University (WNE) seeks applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning in Spring 2027. Candidates for this position must hold a Ph.D. in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Architectural Engineering, or a closely related field, and must demonstrate the ability or potential for excellence in teaching and research at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate is expected to: (1) teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses in construction management, construction engineering, and related courses (3/3 load or 18 credits per year) (2) develop and maintain internationally recognized externally funded research, (3) pursue scholarly and service activities, (4) advise students, and (5) lead national and international student competitions. Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching experience Expertise in construction robotics, automation in construction, smart construction and infrastructure systems, or AI applications in construction. Experience with project-based, laboratory-based, or experiential learning. Experience developing or delivering online, hybrid or technology-enhanced courses in construction management. Industry experience. Experience involving undergraduate students in research. Professional licensure or progress toward professional licensure. The Construction Management Department is housed in the College of Engineering (COE) and offers Bachelor of Science and Master of Science degrees in Construction Management.  The COE offers BS degrees in Civil and Environmental, Mechanical, Industrial, Electrical, Computer, and Biomedical engineering. It also offers MS and PhD degrees in multiple programs. Review of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants are requested to submit a single PDF file containing the following materials: A cover letter, A curriculum vitae, A statement of teaching interests and philosophy A statement of research interests The names and contact information of at least three references. Western New England University is a private, independent, coeducational institution founded in 1919. Located on an attractive 215-acre suburban campus in Springfield, Massachusetts, Western New England University serves 3,900 students, including more than 2,600 full-time undergraduate students. Undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs are offered through Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy, and School of Law. To apply for this position, please submit your materials through the online application. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Candidates for this position must have a Ph.D. in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, or a closely related field, and must have demonstrated ability or potential for excellence in teaching and research at the undergraduate and graduate levels. QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Candidates for this position must have a Ph.D. in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Architectural Engineering,or a closely related field. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/137883": {
      "title": "Information Technolog-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Information Technolog-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Information Technolog-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description About the Role The IT Helpdesk supports students, faculty, and staff with technology issues across campus. As a student Helpdesk Technician, you will be one of the first people users contact when they need assistance. You will work alongside other student employees and full-time IT staff, providing support by phone, email, walk-in visits, classrooms, and offices across campus. No one is expected to know everything on day one. Training is provided, and experienced staff are always available to help. What You Will Do Your exact tasks depend on the shift you are working, but every technician is trained across these areas. Phone and walk-in support Answer calls and greet walk-in visitors, then troubleshoot their issue or route it to the right person. Return missed calls and work through the callback queue, starting with the most urgent requests. Help users with password resets, multi-factor authentication, account lockouts, and other account problems. Troubleshoot Wi-Fi, wired network, and VPN connections, and gather details for the Networking team when an issue needs to go further. Help users get university-supported software installed and running on university and personal devices. Tickets and documentation Log every request in the work order system with clear notes on what was done and what happens next. Follow each ticket through to resolution, or hand it off with full notes if your shift ends first. Judge how urgent each issue is and escalate to full-time staff when it is outside your knowledge or authority. Campus and classroom support Visit classrooms, labs, and offices to fix equipment problems on site. Set up workstations, displays, printers, phones, and other equipment for faculty and staff. Walk through classrooms and labs each week to catch problems before they affect a class. Collect, log, and process electronic waste for recycling. Hardware and device prep Diagnose and repair university-owned computers and replace failed parts. Image computers and prepare them for deployment, including temporary deployments. Keep temporary and deployment stock at target levels and contact users when their devices are ready. Submit warranty claims to Dell for eligible hardware. Schedule and Pay The position pays $15.00 per hour. You set your availability around your classes, and we build your shifts from it using SubItUp, our scheduling system. Period Helpdesk hours Your hours per week Fall and spring semesters Mon to Thu, 8:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.; Fri, 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. 8 to 20 Summer and winter breaks Mon to Fri, 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Up to 40 Availability during breaks is optional, though preferred. Training and Growth Training happens during your regular paid shifts. You will learn our tools, procedures, and troubleshooting methods from full-time staff and experienced student technicians, and you can always ask for help when something is new. Supervisors give regular feedback and coaching. Technicians who show initiative and good judgment are given more responsibility over time. You will leave with hands-on experience in hardware repair, systems support, and customer service that carries over to IT jobs and certifications after graduation. Equal Opportunity Western New England is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We welcome candidates whose backgrounds may contribute to the further diversification of our community. See the University's Notice of Non-Discrimination for details. Qualifications No prior IT experience is needed. We train every new technician on the job and look for someone who is dependable, treats people well, takes initiative, and tries to figure things out for themselves. Required Enrolled as a full-time student at Western New England University (undergraduate or graduate). Available to work at least 8 hours per week during the semester. Comfortable helping people in person and over the phone, including people who are stressed or frustrated. Able to explain technical problems in plain language. Able to handle confidential information, such as student records and account data, with discretion. Reliable about showing up on time and working your full scheduled shifts. Preferred, Not Required Prior experience in IT support, computer repair, or a similar role. Studying information technology or a related field. CompTIA A+ certification. Dell hardware technician certification. Availability to work during summer and winter breaks. Physical Requirements Able to lift and carry computers, monitors, and other equipment weighing up to 35 pounds. Able to walk to classrooms, labs, and offices across campus. Closed-toe shoes on every shift, and professional dress following the Helpdesk dress code. Reasonable accommodations are available. Requests are reviewed by Human Resources together with Student Accessibility Services. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/137509": {
      "title": "Advancement Database Coordinator",
      "description": "Advancement Database Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Advancement Database Coordinator Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $50,000.00 - $58,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Degree Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: The Advancement Database Coordinator is an integral member of the Advancement Division at Western New England University and is responsible for the maintenance and proper use of the Advancement database (CRM Advance) as well as all gift processing procedures. The position manages constituent data and assists in the creation of reports, exports, etc. The Coordinator provides effective support and training to Advancement staff in the use of CRM Advance when necessary. Additionally, this position is responsible for the recording, receipting and acknowledgment of charitable gifts to ensure compliance with financial auditor requirements. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: Expertise in specialized Advancement relational databases and other software, and ability to learn new/emerging technologies Strong technical skillset paired with robust analytical and critical thinking skills Commitment to data integrity and a high level of attention to detail Ability to discretely handle highly sensitive and confidential information including financial information Understanding of the importance of accurate data to the Advancement Division and University ESSENTIAL Job Functions: Process, record and maintain all charitable gifts received to the University, including cash, check, stock transactions, payroll deduction, credit cards, and online transactions. Ensures all gifts, payments and pledges accurately reflect donor intent of gift, payment schedule, credit transaction, gift set, etc. Coordinate with the Vice President for University Advancement, Gift Officers, Controller’s Office, and Advancement Services team as appropriate to ensure proper gift entry and record keeping. Develop and manage processes to identify and record updated constituent data from a variety of sources, including employment information and biographical updates to ensure consistent and accurate information about constituents and donors. Mange all aspects of Matching Gift Program to include confirmations and gift entry. Serves as a liaison to corporate and third-party payment processors. Responsible for immediate receipting of all gifts, as well as the timely production of acknowledgement correspondence. Independently manage the regular flow of constituent data between CRM Advance and our constituent facing website. Ensure that our external facing engagement platform and our enterprise data are in sync with a high level of attention to detail. Maintain accurate procedures for all gift processing duties and collaborate with Associate Director of Advancement Services on policies. This includes daily gift and pledge acceptance and processing, receipting, restricted gifts, pledges, write-offs, noncash gifts, internal controls, record retention and all related documentation, audit documentation, and reconciliation. Possess thorough knowledge of CRM Advance biographical data, identifying areas that need updates and taking initiative to address those areas. Serve as the primary point of entry for biographical information into the CRM Advance database from a variety of sources including Advancement colleagues, campus partners, University and external news sites and publications, and more. Conduct regular data audits to ensure accurate and consistent data to support the Advancement Division needs in the areas of development, alumni relations, and advancement services. Prioritize data hygiene and acquisition projects in alignment with Divisional priorities. Generate a variety of financial reports, on an ad-hoc basis, from the database which reflect contributions to a specific fund, responses to a solicitation, honorary gifts, or other various coded donor attributes. Assist with other giving reports as requested. Communicate regularly with the Payroll Office to support of accuracy of payroll deduction records. Maintain proper backup documentation for all reports. Support other Advancement Division functions such as updates to constituent records and data integrity as they pertain to the annual giving day and crowdfunding campaigns. Support the Associate Director of Advancement Information in developing end-user documentation and conducting staff training for database setup, data entry procedures, and data output procedures in alignment with industry best practices and Advancement/University policies. Proactively communicate with appropriate Advancement colleagues, including the prospect researcher and assigned prospect manager(s), when a significant change takes place with a prospect or donor. Support the Associate Director of Advancement Information in monitoring the health of the database and reporting out on key metrics. Process returned mail and email; research updates in the form of new addresses and employment information from National Change of Address (NCoA) data. Serve as a backup to the Associate Director of Advancement Services in their absence and as needed. Perform other tasks as assigned. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Ability to organize and complete multiple tasks simultaneously, managing time to meet deadlines Willingness to take initiative, keep a positive attitude, and maintain a professional demeanor Excellent interpersonal skills, including verbal and written communication Outstanding attention to detail and commitment to quality and customer service Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues, to work independently, and to accept direction Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and alumni/donor database systems, and ability to learn new systems Detail oriented, flexible in responding to changing priorities, sound judgement, and the ability to work with highly confidential and sensitive information Argos experience a plus ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Sitting, standing, bending, walking, climbing stairs, and reaching as expected in normal office setting Occasional lifting, not to exceed 25 pounds Operation of computer keyboard and monitor HOURS: Exempt, 40 hours per week QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience and at least 1 year of experience in a related field required. Knowledge of computers, specifically software used in fundraising programs required. Experience with relational databases such as CRM Advance preferred. Demonstrated project management, communication, organization, and analytical skills. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/137196": {
      "title": "University Events-Student Assistant",
      "description": "University Events-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account University Events-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description All University Events Planning student employees are considered extensions of the full-time staff members, with similar job responsibilities. Student employees will perform a variety of operational support functions that deal with the delivery of various services to the University community, support of events, coordination of non-academic scheduling, and day-to-day operations of various buildings and rooms on Campus. Assists in the delivery of University Events Services for the campus community and booking of events in our Event Scheduling System. Check in on events and make sure things are set up, and at times, you will assist in breaking down and setting up events. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of University Events Planning or the Assistant Director of University Events Planning. The nature of this position and the constantly evolving nature of the event functions on campus require assistance with or performing tasks that may be created and/or modified. Qualifications Individuals must possess the knowledge, skill, and interpersonal abilities commensurate with designated duties or be able to explain and demonstrate performance of the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some other combination of skills and abilities. Ability to follow instructions and procedures, both written and verbal. Ability to work efficiently in a high-traffic office with faculty, staff, administration, and student groups. Ability to use a variety of computer software packages, a computerized reservation system, and basic computer literacy. Ability to perform a high level of customer service using both diplomacy and tact. Ability to work with and cooperate with the Director of University Events Planning and Assistant Director of University Events Planning, and other University staff, faculty, and students. Ability to work independently, organize time, and prioritize assigned tasks. Ability to read, write, and communicate effectively, in writing and over the phone. Ability to perform minor and major set-ups for events and meetings. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135857": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Enrollment Services-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Enrollment Services-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description To provide clerical assistance to the Directors, Specialists, Student Services Administrators, and Receptionists of SAS with a minimum of supervision. Distinguishing Characteristics: Act as clerical support. DESCRIPTION OF DUTIES AND TASKS : Essential Job Functions : · File · Assist with mailings to students and faculty · Basic data entry · Inter-office errands · Other duties as assigned by the Directors, Specialists, Student Services Administrators, and Receptionists Marginal Job Functions : · Operate office machinery Qualifications Ability to file and retrieve data from student files. Good interpersonal skills and the capacity to follow directions. Capacity to adhere strictly to standards of preserving confidentiality of information. Skill in the use of computer systems Good organizational skills Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
