    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135625": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a student worker to assist faculty with preparation and organization of pharmacy laboratory activities.  PharmD students are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities Assist with preparation of materials for pharmacy laboratory activities Prepare mock prescriptions and other instructional materials using faculty-provided information Gather and organize supplies for upcoming laboratory sessions Assist with laboratory inventory organization Restock and organize instructional materials and supplies Assist with setup and breakdown of laboratory activities Complete other laboratory preparation tasks as assigned by faculty Qualifications Qualifications Current WNE student in good academic standing Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Dependable and able to follow written and verbal instructions Ability to work independently Familiarity with pharmacy laboratory activities preferred PharmD students are encouraged to apply. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135616": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a WNE student to assist faculty with preparation and coordination of Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs) and standardized patient activities. Because this position may involve access to confidential assessment materials, applicants cannot be currently enrolled in the PharmD program. Responsibilities Assist with preparation and organization of OSCE materials Assist with preparation of standardized patient training materials Help coordinate communications and materials for standardized patients Review standardized patient instructions for clarity and consistency Organize case materials and supporting documents Assist with scheduling and other administrative aspects of standardized patient activities Assist with in-person or virtual standardized patient training as needed Maintain strict confidentiality of all OSCE cases and assessment materials Complete other OSCE-related preparation tasks as assigned Qualifications Must not be enrolled in the PharmD program or pre-pharmacy Current WNE student in good academic standing Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Strong written and verbal communication skills Dependable and able to work independently Comfortable using Microsoft Office/365 and Zoom Able to maintain strict confidentiality regarding assessment materials Students in health sciences, psychology, biology, neuroscience, education, communication, or other related programs are encouraged to apply. Confidentiality This position may involve access to secure educational assessment materials. The student worker must maintain strict confidentiality and may not share, reproduce, retain, photograph, or discuss OSCE cases or related assessment materials outside of assigned work. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
