    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/132919": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Development/Director of Development",
      "description": "Senior Director of Development/Director of Development You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Director of Development/Director of Development Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $115,000.00 - $145,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Degree Apply Description Western New England University is accepting applications for the position of Senior Director of Development/Director of Development. The position level offered to the selected candidate will be based on experience. The hiring range for this position is: Director of Development (3-5 years of experience) - $100,000 - $125,000 Senior Director of Development (5+ years of experience) - $125,000 - $145,000 PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION : The Senior Development Director/Development Director is responsible for leading all development activities within three colleges or operational units (COU) of the University in effort to raise funding in support of the mission. In coordination with the Vice President for Advancement and other members of the Advancement Team, the position develops, implements and monitors a comprehensive fundraising plan to expand philanthropic support of the organization including strengthening relationships with key donors, identifying and cultivating new prospective donors, engaging with leadership of the CAU to build a strong culture of philanthropy, and working with the members of the Advancement Team to deliver programming that increases engagement and philanthropy. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: This position works closely with the Vice President for Advancement and serves on the senior management team for the Advancement Division. The position requires a collaborative and creative approach to redefining and solving problems, along with identifying alternate strategies that are novel and effective. Responsibilities include: Playing a key leadership role in the University’s fundraising activities, including providing strategic direction based on an analytical review of friend-and-fundraising data and donor behaviors, with special attention paid to creating and implementing strategies that focus on building a robust donor pipeline. Creating and implementing programs to build stronger relationships with alumni, parents, business leaders, faculty, and staff. Cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding of prospects and donors with the capacity to make gifts at all levels. Building strong relationships with colleagues across the University to achieve fundraising objectives. Qualifications QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Seven years of fundraising experience Some management/supervisory experience Experience securing major gifts by strategically managing a portfolio and fostering meaningful relationships Highly developed leadership and organizational skills. A track record of working closely with senior leaders and providing the support necessary to ensure their success in development activities Proven ability to develop guidelines and metrics to track effectiveness of projects and processes Interpersonal skills to establish and maintain good working relationships ranging from senior management to technical and administrative staff Commitment to ethical practices in fundraising Demonstrated ability to manage conflict. Bachelor’s degree required. ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Sitting, standing, bending, walking, climbing stairs, and reaching as expected in normal office setting. Occasional lifting, not to exceed 25 pounds Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/132021": {
      "title": "College of Pharmacy-Student Assistant",
      "description": "College of Pharmacy-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account College of Pharmacy-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Education Level None Apply Description To provide coverage (phone and visitor) for the front desk in the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences during lunch hour, and flexible for additional times as needed. To walk guests back to the Dean’s offices when necessary. The ideal applicant should be customer focused, outgoing, friendly, articulate, and dress in a professional manner.  He/she should not be a Pre-Pharmacy student or in the Pharmacy Program. Qualifications Excellent interpersonal skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to interact effectively in a highly diverse professional environment. Ability to multi-task Must be work-study student. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
