    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/122678": {
      "title": "Head Women's Swim Coach",
      "description": "Head Women's Swim Coach You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Women's Swim Coach Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $8,000.00 - $8,000.00 Commission Position Type Part Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Degree Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: To manage all aspects of an NCAA DIII competitive intercollegiate swim program. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: This is a part-time, head coach position that requires strong organization skills with attention to detail and the ability to work in a fast-paced and ever-changing environment.  Willingness to work a flexible schedule.  Access to confidential student records and confidential donor and budget information. Ability to demonstrate professional coaching competency and knowledge of DIII intercollegiate athletics.  Ability to work with college administration, faculty, staff, students, alumni, media, and various external stakeholders in a professional, courteous, and confidential manner. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Recruiting and retaining student-athletes Practice and game planning and execution Coordinating technical, tactical, and fitness/conditioning training sessions Promoting holistic mental and physical well-being of student-athletes Supervising coaching staff Engaging in the planning and coordination of student-athlete development initiatives including academic progress monitoring, study halls, leadership development program, e.g. Assuring program is in compliance with all Departmental, University, LEC, and NCAA rules, regulations, and policies Participating in oversight of equipment distribution and return Engaging in alumni relations activities Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations including Title IX Excellent leadership and supervisory skills Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrated coaching ability – may include appropriate coaching licensure or certification Ability to work effectively individually and as part of a team The ability to articulate the vision, mission and core values of Division III Athletics and athletics at Western New England University Ability to work collaboratively with athletic department and building staff members as well as with members/staff of other groups/divisions on Campus ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Ability to meet physical requirements of coaching profession – swimming, conducting practices, travel, office work. (Sitting, standing, bending, reaching and lifting) in a moderate athletic environment. Sufficient mobility to independently negotiate the University Campus. HOURS: Nights and Weekends required QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Bachelor’s Degree required; Master’s Degree preferred in Athletic Coaching, Physical Education, Recreation, or associated fields.  A minimum of 3 years of university coaching experience requested.  CPR, First Aid and AED, certification and successful completion of mandated University training is also required. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/128938": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of English",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of English You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of English Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,700.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description The Department of English, Communication, Culture, and Art at Western New England University invites applications to fill openings for Adjunct Professor of English in the fall 2026 semester. The department seeks a candidate who can teach at least two in-person sections of a first-year composition course on Monday/Wednesday/Friday mornings. First-year composition courses focus on teaching critical reading and academic writing skills, including developing a sensitivity to language and writing, mastering citation and documentation skills, and critically assessing one’s own writing as well as that of others. Particular attention is given to the importance of thesis, evidence, audience, and thoughtful revision.   A standard syllabus template and frameworks for required assignments will be provided. Qualifications A Master's degree in a related area is required. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/130051": {
      "title": "Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Education Level None Apply Description This position is responsible for the care and maintenance of laboratory spaces CSP 111, 117, 201, 309, and 409, along with managing lab supply inventory. This role supports the daily operations of academic research and teaching laboratories within the Department of Pharmaceutical & Administrative Sciences. Essential Job Functions Perform routine laboratory tasks as assigned Maintain laboratory equipment and supplies Clean laboratory equipment, including machinery, autoclave, and glassware Conduct inventory of lab supplies and materials Label laboratory materials and equipment appropriately Assist with biohazardous waste organization General cleaning of the laboratory spaces as assigned Qualifications Experience working in an academic research laboratory required Proficiency in Microsoft Word and Excel Excellent verbal and written communication skills Physical Requirements Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/129817": {
      "title": "Golden Hours Programming Assistant",
      "description": "Golden Hours Programming Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Golden Hours Programming Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $16.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Golden Hours Programming Assistant will support planning, coordination, and implementation of campus events during Golden Hours. Golden Hours are Thursday-Saturday evenings between the hours of 8-10pm. This position works closely with the Assistant Director of Student Involvement and Programming to monitor and identify gaps in the programming calendar. The Golden Hours Programming Assistant will help track club programming and provide support to student organizations hosting events by assisting with event communication and operations. Responsibilities: Monitor and track club participation in Golden Hours events. Communicate with student groups on a weekly basis about upcoming events and provide support with planning and logistics as needed. Assist with the setup, execution, and breakdown of events. Serve as an on-site support person during events who helps address issues that may arise and ensure that events run smoothly. Help maintain and review the Student Involvement programming calendar to ensure consistent event coverage during Golden Hours. Identify gaps in scheduled programming and plan or coordinate events to fill open time slots. Provide feedback and ideas for new programs that support student engagement during Golden Hours.   ​ Qualifications Current, full-time WNE undergraduate student with a GPA of 2.8 or higher. Strong organizational and communication skills. Interest in event planning, student engagement, or campus programming. in event planning, student engagement, or campus programming. Ability to work collaboratively with student organizations. Availability to work a minimum of 5 hours per week, primarily during scheduled Golden Hours events (Thursday-Saturday evenings 8-10pm). Strong ability to problem-solve and take initiative in a fast-paced environment. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/129809": {
      "title": "Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharm and Admin Serv-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description Position Summary The Graduate Program Marketing & Recruitment Assistant supports outreach, promotion, and recruitment efforts for the College of Pharmacy’s graduate program offerings. This role assists in developing marketing materials, managing digital and social media presence, coordinating recruitment events, and supporting prospective student engagement to help grow and strengthen graduate program enrollment. Essential Job Functions · Assist in developing and distributing marketing materials · Manage and update content for graduate program social media accounts and website pages · Coordinate with faculty and staff to gather content (student spotlights, program updates, testimonials) for promotional use · Support the creation of graphics, photos, or short videos for recruitment purposes · Perform other marketing and administrative duties as assigned Qualifications Required: · Currently enrolled student in good academic standing · Excellent written and verbal communication skills · Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) · Strong organizational skills and attention to detail · Comfortable engaging with prospective students, faculty, and staff professionally Preferred: · Experience with social media management (Instagram, LinkedIn, Facebook, TikTok) · Familiarity with graphic design tools (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, etc.) · Basic photo/video editing skills Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/125983": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Law (Director of Externship)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Law (Director of Externship) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Law (Director of Externship) Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $105,000.00 - $110,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Faculty Education Level JD Apply Description Western New England University School of Law invites applicants for a tenure track assistant professor of law faculty position with primary responsibility serving as Director of Externships starting August 2027. We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. The Director of Externships, who will work collaboratively with the Associate Dean of Experiential Learning, will be responsible for oversight and management of all aspects of the externship program, including: curriculum for the externship seminars; recruiting, training, supervising and evaluating field supervisors; conducting or coordinating site visits; establishing program policies; representing the law school in local, regional, and national externship meetings; and providing counseling and guidance to students about appropriate placements to develop skills and advance professional goals. This position includes responsibility for expanding the current program for the part-time and evening students in the new JD Access distance learning program. This position also includes the opportunity to enhance the current program, such as launching a semester in practice, summer externship program, creating a seminar to accompany second externships, and contributing more broadly to deepening the law school’s commitment to professional development and experiential learning opportunities. The teaching load for this position is 12 credits, which typically include two 4-credit offerings for the externship program, two credits of a required 1L course dedicated to an introduction to the legal profession, and an additional 2-credit course to be determined in consultation with the Dean. Applicants must possess a J.D. or equivalent degree, a record of academic achievement, and the potential to develop a strong program of scholarly research. Faculty members in the School of Law must also commit to teaching courses in-person and in a distance learning format, remaining current in the scholarly life of the discipline and should carry out professional scholarly activities such as attendance at professional conferences, research, and scholarly writing projects within the discipline.  All applications should include a letter of application, including areas of teaching interest, and a CV that includes a record of publications and/or a scholarly agenda. WNE offers an excellent benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, 403b retirement plan, and tuition remission. We are a student-centered institution committed to preparing graduates for successful and ethical legal careers. Faculty enjoy a collaborative academic community, opportunities for interdisciplinary engagement, and strong support for teaching, scholarship, and service. Located in Springfield, Massachusetts, the School of Law offers small class sizes, a diverse student body, and convenient access to Boston, Hartford, Albany, and the broader New England region. Western New England University is a private, independent, coeducational institution founded in 1919. Located on an attractive 215-acre suburban campus in Springfield, Massachusetts, Western New England University serves 3,800 students, including more than 2,600 full-time undergraduate students. Undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs are offered through Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy, and School of Law. Western New England University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and welcomes applications from all qualified applicants. To apply for this position please visit https://wne.edu/human-resources/careers.cfm For inquiries about this position, please contact Professor Tim Webster, Chair of the Faculty Personnel Committee ( timothy.webster@law.wne.edu ) or Dale-Marie Dahlke, Law School Director of Operations ( dalemarie.dahlke@law.wne.edu ) Qualifications ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: 1.   Course development and classroom teaching. 2.   Advising students on an individual and sometimes confidential basis. 3.   Staying current in the discipline through scholarly research and professional development. 4.   Performing service duties, especially involving membership on committees.  Participation in university governance, together  with effective teaching, advising, and scholarship and professional development, is required for promotion and tenure in the University. 5. Developing programs, and the overall curriculum in the field. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Distinguished academic record, including a JD from an ABA-approved law school or a foreign equivalent. Significant and meaningful practice experience, including a judicial clerkship, is a preferred qualification. Ability to speak to a group of students in a classroom in a residential and distance learning environment. Ability to interact verbally with students in a classroom environment or with individual students in private meetings. Knowledge of the field of study that is sufficiently broad to teach most of the basic courses in the discipline. Sufficient depth of knowledge to teach upper division courses in at least one area of specialization. Ability to use the telephone and E-mail for communication or to use alternate methods for effective communication, including Learning Management Systems platforms for distance learning courses. Ability to grade student exams, term papers, reports and other in-class and outside assignments. Skill in basic computer and web-based technology use and ability to assist students in computer literacy in the field. Ability to meet classes on schedule and to carry out assignments in a prompt and timely fashion. Skill in interpersonal communication sufficient to interact effectively with students, colleagues, and administrators. Skill in reading, analyzing, summarizing and in other ways comprehending and utilizing written academic material Ability to write effectively in internal university communications, in interaction with outside constituencies, and in preparing scholarly and professional material. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/125755": {
      "title": "Director of Total Rewards",
      "description": "Director of Total Rewards You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Total Rewards Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $100,000.00 - $110,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: Western New England University is looking for someone with a builder’s mindset to lead its Total Rewards function. This role would be responsible for developing a redefined integrated Total Rewards program, including compensation, benefits and recognition strategies designed as a strategic lever to attract and retain top talent. Reporting directly to the Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO) and in partnership with senior leadership, constituent stakeholders, and the Board, the person who comes into this role will also effectively oversee day-to-day payroll and benefits operations – meaning they need to be as comfortable in the details as they are at the strategic level. Essential Job Functions Reporting to the CHRO, the Director provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for WNE’s compensation and benefits programs, partnering closely with the Talent Acquisition and HR Business Partner colleagues and other institutional stakeholders to ensure programs are competitive, compliant, equitable and drive performance and culture. Compensation Strategy and Program Development Lead the design and implementation of WNE's formal compensation philosophy, covering base pay, merit, COLA, stipends, bonuses, ensuring market-competitiveness and internal equity. Build a comprehensive job grading and market pricing framework: developing and maintaining job families, grades, and salary bands across faculty and staff populations. Lead compensation processes including merit or COLA increases, equity reviews, and ad hoc adjustment recommendations that align with market-competitiveness and University mission and strategy. Provide expert guidance to hiring managers and HR colleagues on job description development, offer structuring, and compensation decision-making aligned with the compensation philosophy. Partner with the CHRO on executive compensation, including support for Board Compensation Committee work and incentive plan evaluation process. Benefits Strategy and Administration Lead the strategic benefits renewal process in partnership with the CHRO and broker team — evaluating carrier options, plan design, cost management strategies, and alternative funding models. Oversee the Assistant Manager of Benefits Administration and day-to-day benefits administration, including eligibility, enrollment, vendor management, compliance filings, and employee communications. Drive wellness strategy development and programming in partnership with benefit brokers and internal stakeholders. Act as a lead facilitator and coordinator of the Human Resources-led Benefits and Wellness Committees, and as a liaison and primary point of contact for the Personnel Benefits and Administration Committee of the Faculty Senate and to Staff Council on benefits matters. Ensure compliance with ACA, ERISA, PFML, FMLA, and all applicable federal and state regulations. Oversee annual benefits-related filings and audits. Manage relationships with benefits brokers, carriers, and third-party administrators. Payroll Oversight Oversee accurate and timely processing of all employee and student payroll, ensuring compliance with federal and state wage and hour laws. Partner with HRIS and Finance on payroll system configuration, reporting, and process improvement. Lead ongoing optimization of student employment payroll processes and supervisor accountability frameworks. Ensure audit readiness by overseeing annual payroll-related regulatory obligations and internal payroll controls. Team Development and Collaboration Coach and develop team members in benefits and payroll administration — building capability, accountability, and a culture of accuracy and service. Collaborate closely with Talent Acquisition, Employee Relations, and HR Operations colleagues to ensure total rewards programs support the full employee lifecycle. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Experience and Expertise 5-7 years of progressive HR experience with significant depth in compensation strategy, job evaluation methodologies, salary structures, market pricing, pay equity principles, benefits. Experience interpreting compensation survey data and labor market trends (e.g., CUPA-HR, Mercer, Salary.com). Demonstrated experience building or significantly redesigning a compensation program — job architecture, pay grades, market pricing, and annual adjustment processes – as part of an integrated total rewards program, spanning benefits, incentives, and recognition. Strong working knowledge of benefits plan design, vendor management, and regulatory compliance (ACA, ERISA, PFML, FMLA). Experience overseeing payroll operations and working closely with HRIS platforms, leveraging technology solutions where available to minimize manual processes as much as possible. Strong financial acumen to assess program costs, budget impact, and long-term sustainability. Higher education experience preferred but not required — what matters more is the ability to learn a complex, relationship-driven environment quickly and operate with appropriate nuance. CCP preferred; CBP and/or SHRM-SCP a plus. Leadership and Presence Ability to guide organizational change related to pay structures, workforce planning, or program redesign. Confident, credible, and composed in front of senior leaders, faculty governance bodies, and the Board — this role requires the ability to present compensation data and recommendations with authority and clarity Demonstrated leadership skills, including team management, coaching, and development of HR professionals. Highly collaborative working style with the ability to build trust across a complex, multi-constituent institution ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Sitting, bending and reaching as expected in a normal office setting. Occasional lifting not expected to exceed 25 pounds. Operation of computer keyboard. Operation of calculator. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/125299": {
      "title": "Operations Assistant, Admissions",
      "description": "Operations Assistant, Admissions You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Operations Assistant, Admissions Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $17.60 - $20.60 Hourly Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level High School Diploma or GED/HiSET Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: The purpose of this position is to provide administrative support to the Office of Admissions. The primary responsibilities include establishing and maintaining data in the customer relationship management (CRM) computer system used by the Office of Admissions, maintaining electronic and/or paper files for prospective students, processing mail and materials received by and sent from the Office of Admissions, and assisting with projects as assigned. The position also includes responsibility to provide coverage for the Office of Admissions receptionist and the University switchboard operator, as assigned. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: It is essential that the individual have demonstrate a strong attention to detail and accuracy and be willing to assist with and share responsibility for tasks and projects across the Operations team support staff.  It is also essential that the individual be able to work with data and information in a confidential manner. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Please list in order of importance, with the first duty being the most important. Develop and maintain proficiency in the Office of Admissions system. Develop proficiency in other systems used by the Office of Admissions, such as the student information system, as applicable for assigned projects. Enter prospective student data into the system in an accurate and timely manner. This includes, but is not limited to, entry of inquiries, applicant data and applicant materials, and processing deposits. Maintain student data in the system based upon documentation or information received for students’ records or based upon projects assigned. Process student applications. Enter relevant information into the system, prepare necessary paper and / or electronic files for the student, and route to appropriate individual(s) as necessary based upon status of the student file. Process supporting materials related to prospective student inquiries and applications. Run basic reports and perform searches within the system. Prepare and / or assist with preparation of various daily, weekly, monthly, and ad hoc reporting. Process incoming mail for the Office of Admissions, including routing of mail to appropriate individuals within the office. Process outgoing direct mail including generating mail labels and mailing list files, providing files and direct mail pieces to the mailroom, and addressing direct mail pieces. Process payments for application fees and deposits and route to the appropriate individual(s).  Effectively utilize systems needed to identify and process electronic payments. Accurately and effectively perform various projects as assigned. Share responsibility for providing Saturday morning front office coverage on a rotational basis (which is a shared responsibility of the Operational team support staff members, based upon specific job responsibilities). Serve as a backup, as needed, for the Office of Admissions receptionist and the University switchboard operator.  Answer phones, schedule appointments, greet visitors, answer questions, take messages, and direct calls to the appropriate individual. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Strong attention to detail and accuracy; Ability to accurately proofread data entered into system and electronic / paper documents Previous experience working with Microsoft Office software (primarily Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft Word, and Microsoft Excel) Desire and aptitude to develop strong working knowledge of the Office of Admissions system and supporting administrative systems Desire and aptitude to develop working knowledge of enrollment management concepts and practices Ability and willingness to learn and perform all essential job functions, including utilization of various computer applications, within a reasonable period of time of being introduced to the function Ability to work within a team that requires cross-training of functions and shared responsibility for projects and tasks Ability to work with visitors in a manner that makes them feel welcomed and comfortable; strong customer service skills Ability to work in a professional and cooperative manner with co-workers, colleagues, supervisors, and University guests and visitors Ability to work efficiently, effectively, and meet deadlines Ability to work with personal data in a confidential manner ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Ability to sit and work on a computer for extended periods of time HOURS: Standard University hours – 8:30 am to 4:30 pm, Monday through Friday.  May require evening and weekend hours. QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: High School Diploma required; Bachelor’s degree preferred Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/126900": {
      "title": "Client Engagement Coordinator (Student)",
      "description": "Client Engagement Coordinator (Student) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Client Engagement Coordinator (Student) Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $25.00 Hourly Position Type Student Education Level Not Specified Apply Description Purpose of this Position: The Center for Social Justice (CSJ) is looking for a highly motivated individual to provide key administrative and communications support to its legal programs and office operations. The CSJ operates free legal services programs for the community, including the Consumer Debt Initiative and CORI Sealing & Expungement Project, through which students at WNE Law may gain experiential learning opportunities. The CSJ also serves as a hub for public interest activity and innovative, interdisciplinary research and advocacy at WNE Law. The Client Engagement Coordinator will work closely with the CSJ Director, Staff Attorney, law students, volunteers, and clients, exercising sound judgment, maintaining strict confidentiality, and managing multiple priorities in a faced-past legal and academic setting. Essential Job Functions: The Client Engagement Coordinator ensures that the CSJ maintains timely and accurate communication with active clients as well as community members who contact our office for assistance. This entails coordinating both ingoing and outgoing communications through multiple channels. The Client Engagement Coordinator communicates professionally, compassionately, and respectfully. Additionally, the Client Engagement Coordinator also ensures that the CSJ is telling its story effectively to target audiences, thereby generating visibility, building community, and maintaining engagement. Client Engagement: · Manage incoming and outgoing communications from CSJ office phone and organizational email. · Conduct client intake, eligibility screening, and referral coordination. · Coordinate appointments, follow-up and reminder communications, and case-related administrative processes. · Accurately log data in client management software. · Assist with processing incoming mail and court intakes. · Maintain referral sheet for legal and social services. Community Outreach & Social Media · Operate CSJ social media accounts (Instagram, LinkedIn) · Design content for CSJ social media, website, and other external communications (e.g., newsletter). · Assist CSJ Director in coordinating with WNE communications and marketing teams. · Maintain CSJ alumni database and ensure that students, alumni, and stakeholders remain engaged with CSJ social media. · Help advertise CSJ events and services. · Attend events and clinics when possible. This position is expected to require approximately 18–20 hours per week. Qualifications Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: · Experience providing direct client or customer service, preferably in a nonprofit, legal, healthcare, social services, education, or community-based setting. · Demonstrated understanding of the nature of working with underserved communities. · Effective verbal and written communication skills with a high level of professionalism and care. · Ability to communicate with individuals facing challenging legal circumstances. · Fluency in Spanish is preferred. · Analytical skills, sound judgment, and excellent attention to detail. · Ability to work collaboratively, proactively, and flexibly in a fast-paced legal environment. · Proficiency with Instagram, LinkedIn, Microsoft Office, and Adobe Pro. · Proficiency with Clio, Canva, and/or generative AI is a plus. Application Requirements: Please submit a resume and cover letter with your application. Candidates should be prepared to provide an unofficial transcript and at least two professional references upon request. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/123860": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Residence Life",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Residence Life You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director of Residence Life Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $54,000.00 - $56,000.00 Salary Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE AND DESCRIPTION OF THIS POSITION: The Assistant Director of Residence Life is a full-time, live-in professional staff member responsible for providing leadership and oversight for residential education, student engagement, staff supervision, crisis response, and residential operations within a comprehensive residential campus environment. This position supports the mission of the university and the Division of Student Life by fostering inclusive, student-centered residential communities that promote belonging, personal growth, academic success, wellness, and student retention. The Assistant Director provides direct supervision and leadership to professional and student staff and assists with the overall administration of residential communities and departmental initiatives. This position is responsible for overseeing residential education efforts, student conduct processes, crisis management, staff development, occupancy and operational functions, and collaborative campus partnerships. The Assistant Director contributes to departmental strategic planning, assessment initiatives, policy development, and ongoing efforts to enhance the residential student experience. As a member of the Residence Life leadership team, the Assistant Director participates in an on-call rotation and responds to emergencies and critical incidents outside of standard business hours. Evening and weekend responsibilities are required throughout the academic year. In addition to salary and benefits, this position includes a furnished on-campus apartment with utilities, access to laundry facilities, a staff meal plan during the academic year, and professional development opportunities. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Residential Education and Student Development Provide leadership for the development and implementation of a comprehensive residential education model focused on student engagement, belonging, academic success, wellness, and community responsibility. Foster inclusive living-learning environments that support justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion initiatives within residential communities. Oversee community development efforts, educational programming, and student leadership opportunities within assigned residential areas. Support student success and retention efforts through intentional student outreach, intervention, and referrals. Advise student groups, including Residence Hall Council and residential leadership initiatives. Staff Supervision and Development Provide direct supervision, mentorship, training, and evaluation for professional staff, graduate assistants, Head Resident Advisors, and Resident Advisors. Coordinate staff recruitment, selection, onboarding, training, scheduling, and ongoing professional development initiatives. Establish accountability measures and performance expectations for residential staff. Facilitate regular staff meetings, one-on-one supervision meetings, and developmental coaching conversations. Support the development of student leaders through mentoring, conflict resolution, and leadership education. Crisis Response and Student Support Serve in an on-call rotation and respond to emergencies, crises, behavioral concerns, and critical incidents impacting residential students and communities. Provide leadership and coordination in complex student situations involving mental health concerns, student safety, hospital transports, community disruptions, and behavioral interventions. Collaborate with Public Safety, Health and Well-Being, Student Conduct, Title IX, Counseling Services, and other campus partners to support students of concern. Maintain accurate documentation and follow-up related to incidents, student outreach, and crisis response efforts. Participate in university emergency response protocols and behavioral intervention processes as assigned. Student Conduct and Conflict Resolution Serve as a hearing officer for Student Conduct & Community Standards cases. Adjudicate alleged violations of university policies and residential community standards. Facilitate restorative practices, mediation, and conflict resolution processes among students and residential communities. Educate students regarding university expectations, accountability, and community responsibility. Ensure consistency and equity in conduct processes and student interactions. Residential Operations and Facilities Management Oversee day-to-day operations within assigned residential communities, including occupancy management, room changes, facilities concerns, and community safety initiatives. Coordinate opening, closing, break housing, move-in, move-out, and transition processes for residential students. Conduct regular facility walkthroughs and collaborate with Facilities and Public Safety to address maintenance, safety, and security concerns. Monitor occupancy reports, vacancy management, health and safety inspections, work orders, inventories, and damage billing processes. Utilize university systems and databases including The Housing Director (THD), Guardian, Microsoft Office, and other institutional software platforms. Assessment, Administration, and Strategic Initiatives Assist with departmental assessment initiatives and utilize data to improve residential programs, student engagement, and operational effectiveness. Contribute to the development and implementation of departmental policies, procedures, and strategic goals. Track and manage assigned budgets related to residential programming, student leadership initiatives, and operational areas. Prepare reports, maintain records, and provide data analysis related to residential operations and student success initiatives. Serve on departmental, divisional, and university committees and working groups. Support departmental initiatives related to student retention, belonging, and campus climate. Collaboration and Campus Engagement Develop collaborative relationships with campus partners including Academic Affairs, Admissions, Athletics, Counseling Services, Title IX, Student Conduct, Public Safety, and other university departments. Participate in major university events including Orientation, Open Houses, Homecoming, Family Weekend, Senior Week, and Commencement activities. Represent Residence Life and Student Life in university committees, initiatives, and campus-wide programs. Support divisional and institutional priorities through active participation and leadership Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Strong understanding of student development theory, residential education, and student engagement practices. Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and develop professional and student staff. Experience responding to crises, emergencies, and complex student situations with professionalism and sound judgment. Knowledge of student conduct practices, conflict resolution, and restorative approaches. Ability to foster inclusive communities and incorporate justice, equity, diversity, and inclusion principles into daily work. Strong organizational, administrative, and project management skills. Ability to balance multiple priorities in a fast-paced and dynamic environment. Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with diverse campus stakeholders. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and student housing management software systems. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Demonstrated commitment to student success, wellness, and retention. Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field preferred. Bachelor’s degree in a related field required. Minimum of 3–5 years of progressively responsible experience in Residence Life, Housing, Student Affairs, or a related area. Experience supervising professional and/or student staff required. Demonstrated experience with crisis response, student conduct, residential operations, and student engagement initiatives preferred. Experience working within a residential campus environment strongly preferred. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/123456": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Political Science (POSC)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Political Science (POSC) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Political Science (POSC) Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,700.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description Western New England University Department of History, Philosophy, Political Science, and Economics When: Fall 2026 Semester (starts 8/31/2026 ends 12/18/2026) Format: Online asynchronous (LMS: Canvas) Course: POSC 102 Introduction to American National Government (3 cr.) For Fall 2026 (8/31-12/18), we seek an instructor for up to two online asynchronous sections of POSC 102 Introduction to American National Government (30 students are enrolled per section). This course examines the basic structure of the U.S. Constitution and the system of government that it establishes, including federalism, civil liberties, civil rights, government institutions, and citizen participation. The course also focuses on critical analysis of current political events. At minimum, a Master’s in Political Science is required. Please submit a CV and a detailed course syllabus for online asynchronous instruction with your online application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Contact Dr. Meri Clark (413) 796-2264 for further information. Qualifications At minimum, a Master’s in Political Science is required. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/119602": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $100,000.00 - $102,000.00 Salary Position Type Faculty Education Level Doctoral Degree Apply Description Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Position - Mechanical Engineering The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Western New England University invites applications for an immediate opening for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position, beginning in the Spring 2027 semester. Candidates for this position must hold a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or related field with expertise in one of the following areas: Mechatronics/Control Systems, Advanced Manufacturing, Aerospace, Machine Design , or closely related fields. Special consideration will be given to candidates with expertise in artificial intelligence and machine learning applications in mechanical engineering. Industry experience is a plus.  The successful candidate is expected to teach courses at all levels (3/3 load or 18 credits per year), pursue scholarly and externally funded research activities, supervise undergraduate and graduate projects (including PhD), support our innovative first-year engineering program, and provide service to the department and college. We seek outstanding candidates with demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, research, mentoring, and service. The successful candidate will be expected to: Show strong commitment to teaching excellence and student mentorship Develop an externally funded research program in their area of expertise Supervise student research at the undergraduate and graduate levels Establish collaborative relations with local/national industries through industry-sponsored research and projects Contribute to curriculum development and accreditation activities Provide service to the department, college, university, and professional community The preferred start date for the position is the beginning of the Spring 2027 semester but applications for later start dates will also be considered.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Applicants are requested to submit an application package containing the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum vita Statement of teaching and research interests Three references (Names, addresses, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses) Western New England University offers a vibrant undergraduate mechanical engineering program that emphasizes industrially relevant research and design. Additionally, the ME department hosts active Master of Science and PhD programs. The department prides itself on delivering high-quality hands-on engineering education while providing strong mentorship to students. The ME department maintains strong relationships with regional and national industries. For more information about the department, visit: https://wne.edu/academics/undergraduate/mechanical-engineering.cfm Western New England University is a private, independent, coeducational institution founded in 1919. Located on an attractive 215-acre suburban campus in Springfield, Massachusetts, Western New England University serves 3,674 students, including 2,543 full-time undergraduate students, 73 part-time undergraduate students, and 1,058 graduate and professional students. Undergraduate, graduate and professional programs are offered through the Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy and the School of Law. For more information about the University, visit our website at https://wne.edu/ Western New England University offers an excellent benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, 403b retirement plan, and tuition remission. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Candidates for this position must hold a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or related field with expertise in one of the following areas: Mechatronics/Control Systems, Advanced Manufacturing, Aerospace, Machine Design , or closely related fields. Industry experience is a plus. QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Candidates for this position must have a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/120302": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Law",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Law You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Professor of Law Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $105,000.00 - $110,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Faculty Apply Description Western New England University School of Law invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position beginning in the 2027–2028 academic year. We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship to teach Contracts or Civil Procedure as well as one or more business law courses, such as Business Organizations, Secured Transactions, or UCC courses.  The teaching load is 12 to 13 credits per academic year. Applicants must possess a J.D. or equivalent degree, a record of academic achievement, and the potential to develop a strong program of scholarly research. Faculty members in the School of Law must also commit to teaching courses in-person and in a distance learning format, remaining current in the scholarly life of the discipline and should carry out professional scholarly activities such as attendance at professional conferences, research, and scholarly writing projects within the discipline.  All applications should include a letter of application, including areas of teaching interest, and a CV that includes a record of publications and/or a scholarly agenda. WNE offers an excellent benefits package that includes, health, dental, vision, 403b retirement plan, and tuition remission. We are a student-centered institution committed to preparing graduates for successful and ethical legal careers. Faculty enjoy a collaborative academic community, opportunities for interdisciplinary engagement, and strong support for teaching, scholarship, and service. Located in Springfield, Massachusetts, the School of Law offers small class sizes, a diverse student body, and convenient access to Boston, Hartford, Albany, and the broader New England region. Western New England University is a private, independent, coeducational institution founded in 1919. Located on an attractive 215-acre suburban campus in Springfield, Massachusetts, Western New England University serves 3,800 students, including more than 2,600 full-time undergraduate students. Undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs are offered through Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy, and School of Law. For inquiries about this position, please contact Professor Tim Webster, Chair of the Faculty Personnel Committee ( timothy.webster@law.wne.edu ) or Dale-Marie Dahlke, Law School Operations Officer ( dalemarie.dahlke@law.wne.edu ). Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Distinguished academic record, including a JD from an ABA-approved law school or a foreign equivalent. Significant and meaningful practice experience, including a judicial clerkship, is a preferred qualification. Ability to speak to a group of students in a classroom in a residential and distance learning environment. Ability to interact verbally with students in a classroom environment or with individual students in private meetings. Knowledge of the field of study that is sufficiently broad to teach most of the basic courses in the discipline. Sufficient depth of knowledge to teach upper division courses in at least one area of specialization. Ability to use the telephone and E-mail for communication or to use alternate methods for effective communication, including Learning Management Systems platforms for distance learning courses. Ability to grade student exams, term papers, reports and other in-class and outside assignments. Skill in basic computer and web-based technology use and ability to assist students in computer literacy in the field. Ability to meet classes on schedule and to carry out assignments in a prompt and timely fashion. Skill in interpersonal communication sufficient to interact effectively with students, colleagues, and administrators. Skill in reading, analyzing, summarizing and in other ways comprehending and utilizing written academic material Ability to write effectively in internal university communications, in interaction with outside constituencies, and in preparing scholarly and professional material. ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Typical office setting HOURS: Classes are generally held on campus in-person and virtually online during the day, but all faculty members must also teach in the evening division on a regular basis including the distance education program.  Faculty are required to meet all classes as scheduled and to keep regular office hours at times that are mutually convenient for the student and instructor. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/118783": {
      "title": "Vice President for Workforce Development & Community Partnerships",
      "description": "Vice President for Workforce Development & Community Partnerships You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Vice President for Workforce Development & Community Partnerships Apply Overview Salary Range $160,000.00 - $182,000.00 Salary Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: The Vice President of Workforce Development and Community Partnerships serves as a liaison between the University and surrounding local, regional and national communities, including corporate, non-profit, government, military, K-12 schools, and higher-education entities in order to build strategic relationships that advance the University’s civic and economic mission and generate new revenue. This is accomplished through two core areas: (1) developing and delivering workforce development and continuing education programs that align the university's educational offerings with regional economic and labor market needs; and (2) generating value and revenue from the University’s specialized research assets, facilities, and faculty expertise through corporate and industry partnerships. It is expected that the VP will interact extensively with University colleagues, including Academic Affairs, Advancement, Enrollment, and Marketing, Government and External Affairs. This role focuses on revenue-generating partnerships and workforce programming and talent pipeline initiatives, working in close collaboration with – but distinct from – the University’s government relations, advancement, and external communications functions. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: Strategic Leadership: Shape the vision for the university's workforce development initiatives, aligning non-credit and credit-bearing programs to regional industry demands. Drive the cultural and operational change needed to ensure the University consistently delivers on its partnership commitments, building cross-functional accountability so that external promises are matched by reliable internal execution. Employer Engagement: Cultivate partnerships with business leaders, industry associations, and local/state economic development boards to identify workforce needs and develop data-informed and market-responsive offerings, including targeted training, talent and innovation solutions. Budget & Resource Management: Secure external funding, through partnership agreements and grant proposals, for workforce and community education initiatives. Exhibit strong fiscal oversight and build the necessary systems and processes with personnel in order to deliver those designed/developed programs. Program Oversight: Working with Academic Affairs and Enrollment, manage operations spanning corporate training, continuing education, certificate programs, extension/off-campus programming, and online/hybrid programming. Revenue Strategy and Accountability: Establish revenue targets and key performance metrics for workforce development and partnership activities, with accountability for meeting defined annual revenue goals. Report regularly on progress, pipeline, and return on investment. Asset and Innovation Commercialization: Develop and execute strategies to generate value and revenue from University’s specialized research assets, equipment, and facilities (e.g., strategic investments in quantum computing capabilities, Biopharmaceutical technologies, and other grant-funded programs). Partner with academic and research leaders, faculty, and external industry partners to put these assets to productive use through corporate partnerships, applied research collaborations, sponsored use, and innovation initiatives. Partner Engagement: Cultivate relationships with community colleges, high schools, and vocational schools to increase the pipeline of students attending WNE through workforce development programming. Engage campus partners to ensure that necessary programs and transfer agreements are in place. Business Development & Revenue-Generation: Develop and execute a business development strategy that grows revenue through corporate training, continuing education, workforce development programs, facility and laboratory utilization, and strategic industry partnerships. Identify, cultivate, and secure new corporate clients and partners, negotiating agreements that create mutually beneficial educational, workforce, research, and innovation opportunities. WNE offers an excellent benefits package that includes, health, dental, vision, 403b retirement plan, and tuition remission. In addition, ​​this role is eligible for performance-based bonuses tied to net-revenue generation. Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILL AND ABILITIES: Education: A Master's degree in educational administration, adult education, business, or a related field; Doctorate or equivalent combination of senior industry experience is valued. Experience: 10+ years of progressive senior leadership experience in higher education or business development environments, with an understanding of adult learning and corporate training and workforce needs. Key Skills: Labor market analysis, grant administration, financial management, communications, and strategic partnership building. Proven ability to identify market opportunities and build a pipeline of organizational partners and clients. Experience negotiating partnership agreements, service contracts, sponsorships, or other revenue-generating arrangements. Strong execution skills to bring ideas to fruition, including establishing partnerships and working cross-functionally to ensure internal operations are prepared to deliver. Strong collaboration and communication skills, including change leadership. ​​​​​ PHYSICAL AND ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: This position operates primarily in a professional office and meeting environment and requires the ability to perform sedentary work, including extended periods of sitting, computer use, and reading. The role requires frequent communication and the ability to exchange accurate information with internal and external partners in person, by phone, and through virtual platforms. Regular local, regional, and occasional broader national travel may be required to cultivate and maintain partnerships, including the ability to travel to corporate, community, and partner sites. The role requires the ability to attend events and meetings that may occur outside standard business hours, including evenings and occasional weekends. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this role. HOURS: Exempt, hours as needed to complete job responsibilities. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/118257": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of English",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of English You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of English Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,700.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description The Department of English, Communication, Culture, and Art at Western New England University invites applications to fill openings for Adjunct Professor of English in the fall 2026 semester. The department seeks a candidate who can teach at least two in-person sections of a first-year composition course. First-year composition courses focus on teaching critical reading and academic writing skills, including developing a sensitivity to language and writing, mastering citation and documentation skills, and critically assessing one’s own writing as well as that of others. Particular attention is given to the importance of thesis, evidence, audience, and thoughtful revision. Courses are scheduled either three days per week (MWF) for 50 minutes or two days per week (MW or TTH) for 80 minutes. A standard syllabus template and frameworks for required assignments will be provided. Qualifications Successful candidates must have at least a Master’s degree in English, Composition, or a related subject; prior experience teaching undergraduate students; and a demonstrable dedication to student success. Western New England University is a private, independent, coeducational institution founded in 1919. Located on an attractive 215-acre suburban campus in Springfield, Massachusetts, Western New England University serves 3,900 students, including more than 2,600 full-time undergraduate students. Undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs are offered through Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy, and School of Law. For more information about the University, visit our website at http://www.wne.edu . Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/110974": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Biology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Biology Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,700.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Apply Description The Department of Physical & Biological Sciences at Western New England University seeks applications for an adjunct faculty position in Biology beginning in late August 2026. Candidates should have a Master’s degree in biology or related field, previous teaching experience is preferred. Responsibilities include teaching lecture and/or laboratory sections of either general biology or anatomy and physiology. Candidates with the ability to teach evening labs (5:30 – 8:30 PM) are needed. To apply, please submit a current CV and contact information for three references who are able to comment on your ability to teach introductory chemistry. Candidates should submit their materials as soon as possible, however, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Qualifications Candidates should have a Master’s degree in biology or related field, previous teaching experience is preferred. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/106987": {
      "title": "Law School Library-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Law School Library-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Law School Library-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Law Library is seeking several students to work various shifts at the circulation desk. Primary duties include, but are not limited to: staffing the circulation desk, handling circulation transactions, familiarity with circulation and reserve polices, re-shelving library material, registering new patrons, collecting fines, filing loose-leaf release, answering basic directional questions, performing shelf-reading of stacks, and handling short-term projects Essential Job Functions: Handle Circulation Desk activities, including checking materials out and in, registering new patrons, and resetting PINs through the Library's integrated library system. Assist patrons with printing issues, including clearing paper jams, replacing toner, adding money to Phares accounts, and issuing printing cards to patrons not affiliated with the University. Answer the telephone at the Circulation Desk; provide answers to basic questions and refer other inquiries to the appropriate Library staff member. Shelve/reshelve materials in proper place, shelf, file, etc. Open and close the library, including opening or locking doors, and shutting down equipment, etc. Collect fines, and other monies owed and record information properly in both the patron's account and the written log. Update materials by filing looseleaf releases and pocket parts. Other projects as assigned. Qualifications KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS and ABILITIES: Strong ability to follow detailed written and oral instructions. Very good oral communication and interpersonal skills. Attention to detail. COMPETENCIES: Critical Thinking/Problem Solving: Exercise sound reasoning to analyze issues, make decisions. and overcome problems. Teamwork/Collaboration: Build collaborative relationships with colleagues and customers representing diverse cultures, races, ages, genders, religions, lifestyles, and viewpoints. The individual is able to work within a team structure, and can negotiate and manage conflict. Digital Technology: Leverage existing digital technologies ethically and efficiently to solve problems, complete tasks, and accomplish goals. The individual demonstrates effective adaptability to new and emerging technologies. Professionalism/Work Ethic: Demonstrate personal accountability and effective work habits, e.g., punctuality, working productively with others, and time workload management, and understand the impact of non-verbal communication on professional work image. The individual demonstrates integrity and ethical behavior, acts responsibly with the interests of the larger community in mind, and is able to learn from his/her mistakes. ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Lifting books and stretching/stooping or using step stool. Sitting and standing. Lifting and unpacking boxes delivered in the mail. 4) Pushing book trucks that weigh up to 75 lbs. QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Previous customer relations experience preferred. Previous library experience preferred. Minimal typing skills. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/106784": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Communication",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Communication You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Communication Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,900.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description Adjunct Professor of Communication The Department of English, Communication, Culture, and Art at Western New England University invites applications to fill an opening for Adjunct Professor of Communication in the Spring 2027 semester. The department seeks a candidate who can teach at least one in-person section of a junior-level Event Planning course. Courses are scheduled three days per week (MWF) for 50 minutes. The ideal candidate will have at least a Master’s degree in public relations, communication, journalism, or a related subject or at least 10 years’ recent professional experience in the field of communication; prior experience teaching and/or guest-lecturing to undergraduate students; and a demonstrable dedication to student success. The successful candidate may also be asked to teach additional courses in introductory-level communication classes. Applications: Interested candidates should submit a brief cover letter and curriculum vitae to the appropriate job posting online application. Applications completed by September 30, 2026, will receive full consideration. Please contact Dr. Lisa Mastrangelo ( lisa.mastrangelo@wne.edu ) with questions about the position or the search process. Qualifications Qualifications: Candidates must have, at minimum, a Master’s degree in public relations, communication, journalism, or a related subject or at least 10 years’ recent professional experience in event planning theory and practice; and prior experience teaching and/or guest-lecturing to undergraduate students . Candidates who will contribute to diversity on campus, in all its forms, are especially welcome to apply. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
