      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Chemistry You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Chemistry Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,900.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description The Department of Physical & Biological Sciences at Western New England University seeks applications for an adjunct faculty position in Chemistry beginning in late August 2026. Candidates should have a Master’s degree in chemistry or related field, previous teaching experience is preferred. Responsibilities include teaching laboratory sections of organic chemistry or lecture and/or laboratory sections of general chemistry. To apply, please submit a current CV and contact information for three references who are able to comment on your ability to teach introductory chemistry.  Candidates should submit their materials as soon as possible, however, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Qualifications Candidates should have a Master’s degree in chemistry or related field, previous teaching experience is preferred. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
