    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/98452": {
      "title": "Grant Student - BAI, SHUHUA",
      "description": "Grant Student - BAI, SHUHUA You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Grant Student - BAI, SHUHUA Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $20.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description Purpose of this Position: We are seeking highly motivated undergraduate students to join our research team and gain valuable hands-on experience in cutting-edge pharmaceutical science. This opportunity is ideal for students interested in contributing to innovative projects supported by USDA funding, particularly in the development and testing of nanomedicines derived from natural products. Distinguishing Characteristics: Strong attention to detail, reliability, and excellent organizational skills Willingness to learn and follow laboratory protocols Ability to work both independently and as part of a team Essential Job Functions: Participate in the design, preparation, and testing of nanomedicine formulations Support ongoing experiments and perform routine laboratory tasks Maintain accurate laboratory records and document experimental data Assist in data entry and analysis, and help interpret findings under faculty guidance Qualifications Required Knowledge, Skill, and Abilities: Previous laboratory experience is a plus but not required – training will be provided Ergonomic Requirements: Standing for extended periods while performing laboratory procedures Repetitive hand and arm movements for tasks such as pipetting, weighing, and sample preparation Working at a computer for data entry and analysis Wearing appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE), including gloves, lab coat, and safety goggles Hours: 10 - 20 hours per week (flexible scheduling) Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
