    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/96784": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Mathematics",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Mathematics You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Mathematics Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,900.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description The Department of Mathematics at Western New England University is seeking applications from candidates interested in joining us to teach first-year Mathematics courses in person on a part-time basis starting in Fall 2026.  All 100-level courses have a maximum enrollment cap of 30 students per section.  Adjunct faculty who are effective teachers and can provide high quality in person instruction are needed to teach 3-credit undergraduate courses that include Math for Elementary Education, Precalculus Mathematics, Analysis for Business and Economics, Mathematical Reasoning, Introduction to Probability and Statistics, and Calculus. If interested, please include a brief cover letter, current resume, or curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references who can comment on your experience in teaching undergraduate courses.  Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Qualifications We are seeking individuals with at least a Master’s degree, experience in teaching mathematics at the college level, ability to work effectively with diverse groups of students, and flexibility in scheduling. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/93380": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice and Assistant Dean of Experiential Affairs",
      "description": "Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice and Assistant Dean of Experiential Affairs You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Clinical Professor of Pharmacy Practice and Assistant Dean of Experiential Affairs Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $120,000.00 - $150,000.00 Base+Commission/year Position Type Faculty Education Level Doctoral Degree Apply Description Type: Full-Time Category: Pharmacy Experiential Affairs Base Salary Range: $99,761.00 - $123,000 plus administrative stipend Position Title: Executive Director or Assistant Dean of Experiential Affairs Faculty Rank: Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor Education Level: PharmD Western New England University Springfield, Massachusetts Western New England University invites applications for a leadership position in experiential education within the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences. The title will be Executive Director of Experiential Affairs or Assistant Dean of Experiential Affairs, depending on the experience and qualifications of the candidate. The faculty appointment will be at the Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor level (non-tenure track). Position Description The candidate will provide leadership and oversight for the experiential education program within the Doctor of Pharmacy curriculum. Experiential education is a core component of the program and includes both Introductory Pharmacy Practice Experiences (IPPEs) and Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiences (APPEs) across a variety of healthcare settings. The position will work collaboratively with faculty, preceptors, administrators, and healthcare partners to ensure the continued development, quality, and accreditation compliance of experiential training opportunities. This position includes both administrative leadership and faculty responsibilities. Approximately 75% of the workload is dedicated to administration of the experiential education program, including oversight of IPPE and APPE experiences, development of experiential practice sites, preceptor development, and program assessment. The remaining 25% of the workload is allocated to faculty responsibilities, including teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with the expectations of faculty at Western New England University. The teaching expectation is approximately one course (or equivalent credit load) per academic year. The position will also serve as Instructor of Record for experiential education courses within the PharmD curriculum. The position oversees coordination of experiential partnerships associated with the Distance Learning Pathway located throughout the United States and Puerto Rico, as well as international experiential rotations including the interprofessional APPE program in Ghana. Primary Responsibilities Leadership and administration of the experiential education program within the PharmD curriculum Oversight of the planning, implementation, and evaluation of IPPE and APPE rotations Development and maintenance of experiential practice sites and partnerships Coordination of student placement in experiential rotations with faculty and preceptors Development and implementation of preceptor training and development activities Ensuring compliance with accreditation standards and experiential program requirements Participation in teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with a faculty appointment Qualifications Applicants must possess: A PharmD and eligibility for pharmacist licensure in Massachusetts (or ability to obtain licensure in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts) Experience in experiential education, clinical practice, or academic leadership Evidence of teaching, scholarship, and professional service appropriate for appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level Experience with experiential program administration, accreditation processes, and preceptor development is preferred. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. at time of hire. Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level. WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/64763": {
      "title": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Clinical Adjunct Faculty Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $5,000.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Doctoral Degree Apply Description Clinical Adjunct Faculty Position (Department of Psychology, Behavior Analysis Graduate Programs) The Department of Psychology at Western New England University invites applications for a clinical adjunct faculty appointment. This individual will serve as faculty advisor for students in the Behavior Analysis graduate programs (M.S. in Applied Behavior Analysis and/or Ph.D. in Behavior Analysis) and teach graduate courses as assigned by the program director.  Advisors function as mentors and agree to oversee the professional development of the student and to supervise research and completion of other program requirements. Successful candidates will hold a Ph.D. in Behavior Analysis or a related area and demonstrate a record of published research, experience mentoring graduate students, and excellence in teaching. Qualifications Successful candidates will hold a Ph.D. in Behavior Analysis or a related area and demonstrate a record of published research, experience mentoring graduate students, and excellence in teaching. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
