    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/425": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Biomedical Engineering You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty, Biomedical Engineering Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $2,400.00 - $5,000.00 Salary Position Type Adjunct Apply Description PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION: Teach courses and laboratories in Biomedical Engineering ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: Perform the functions of a faculty member in classroom and laboratory settings. Qualifications Post-graduate degree in biomedical engineering, (other) engineering, a related science/technology discipline or a clinical discipline. Western New England University (WNE) is a private, nationally ranked, comprehensive institution with a focus on preparing work-ready and world-ready graduates. Founded in 1919 in Springfield, Massachusetts as a division of Northeastern College, WNE’s 215-acre suburban campus serves more than 3,700 students, including over 2,500 full-time undergraduates. More than 47,000 alumni have earned degrees through its 90+ undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs at Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, and Pharmacy and Health Sciences, and School of Law. Students come from 39 U.S. states and territories and 23 countries. Of 45,104 living alumni, 30% remain within the region, residing in the four Western Massachusetts counties and northern Connecticut. WNE is classified among nationally ranked universities in US News and World Report , and among the Top 100 Undergraduate Engineering programs, and in the Doctoral/Professional Universities category in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education . Western New England University is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  We welcome candidates whose background may contribute to the further diversification of our community. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/139011": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty of Neuroscience",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty of Neuroscience You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty of Neuroscience Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,100.00 - $3,700.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Education Level Master's Degree Apply Description Adjunct Faculty – Neuroscience Western New England University | College of Arts and Sciences The College of Arts and Sciences at Western New England University seeks applications for adjunct faculty in Neuroscience beginning in Spring 2027. We are looking for engaging and effective instructors to provide high-quality undergraduate instruction in the University's interdisciplinary Neuroscience program. Immediate Spring 2027 teaching needs include: • Sensation and Perception • Cognitive Neuroscience • Neurodevelopment • Upper-level Neuroscience electives or special topics We are also interested in developing an adjunct pool of candidates with expertise to teach other courses within the Neuroscience curriculum, including Introduction to Behavioral Neuroscience, Research Methods in Neuroscience, Neurobiology, Genetic and Molecular Neuroscience, Neuropharmacology/Neurobiology of Addiction, and other advanced topics in behavioral, cognitive, cellular, molecular, developmental, or applied neuroscience. Candidates may be considered for one or more courses based on their expertise, availability, and program needs. Experience with undergraduate research, laboratory instruction, or mentoring is welcomed but is not required for all assignments. To apply, please submit a current CV or resume, identify the courses or areas of Neuroscience you are qualified to teach and your Spring availability, and provide contact information for three professional references who can comment on your ability to teach undergraduate students. Candidates should submit materials as soon as possible. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until Spring 2027 teaching needs are filled, and qualified applicants may also be considered for future Neuroscience adjunct opportunities. Qualifications Applicants should have at least a Master's degree in Neuroscience, Psychology, Biology, Biomedical Science, Pharmacology, or a closely related field. A Ph.D. or other appropriate terminal degree is preferred for upper-level courses. Previous college-level teaching experience is preferred. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
